minimum or maximum size of melodic
intervals. This rule expects arguments as
keyword arguments, and that way you can
select which arguments you actually
specify, e.g., the maximum interval (1),
the minimum interval (change the
argument at (1)), or both (2).
The interval size can also change over
time, defined by a BPF (3)." (om-make-point 252 195) (quote "The rule min/max-interval controls the$minimum or maximum size of melodic$intervals. This rule expects arguments $as keyword arguments, and that way $you can select which arguments you$actually specify, e.g., the maximum $interval (1), the minimum interval $(change the argument at (1)), or both $(2).$$The interval size can also change over$time, defined by a BPF (3).") "" (om-make-point 576 355) nil (om-make-color 0 0 0) (om-make-font "Verdana" 12 :family "Verdana" :style (quote (:plain)) :mode (quote nil))))) (when (fboundp (quote set-active)) (set-active box nil)) box))) (quote ((3 0 2 2 nil 0) (6 0 5 1 nil 0) (7 0 5 2 nil 0) (10 0 9 1 nil 0) (11 0 9 2 nil 0) (12 0 9 3 nil 0) (13 0 14 0 nil 0) (14 0 15 0 nil 0) (2 0 15 1 nil 0) (18 0 15 2 nil 0) (13 0 17 0 nil 0) (16 0 17 1 nil 0) (17 0 18 0 nil 0) (5 0 18 1 nil 0) (9 0 18 2 nil 0) (0 0 19 0 nil 0) (15 0 19 3 nil 0) (20 0 19 8 nil 0) (19 0 21 1 nil 0))) nil 8.0))
